#. type: Title-text
#: ../scene.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "A function"
msgstr "Una funzione"

#. type: Resume-text
#: ../scene.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create a function in order to make your program shorter."
msgstr "Crea una funzione per abbreviare il programma."

#. type: ScriptName-text
#: ../scene.txt:3
#, no-wrap
msgid "Move"
msgstr "Move"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Exercise"
msgstr "Esercizio"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The <a object|bottr>bot</a> must pass over all the <a object|waypoint>blue "
"crosses</a> on the ground. The way that must be covered is made of two "
"squares. The first one measures 15 meters, the second 25 meters."
msgstr ""
"Il <a object|bottr>robot</a> deve attraversare tutte le <a "
"object|waypoint>croci blu</a>. Il percorso forma due quadrati, uno di 15 "
"metri di lato e l’altro di 25."

#. type: Image filename
#: ../help/help.E.txt:4
#, no-wrap
msgid "tproc1a"
msgstr "tproc1a"

#. type: \b; header
#: ../help/help.E.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "General principle"
msgstr "Principio generale"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:6
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In order to solve this problem, the most efficient solution consists in "
"creating a <a cbot|function>function</a> that instructs the bot to move on a"
" square shape of a certain size. The main program becomes then very "
"simple:<c/>"
msgstr ""
"La soluzione più efficiente è una <a cbot|function>funzione</a> che faccia "
"percorrere un quadrato della dimensione specificata. Il programma principale"
" diventa semplicissimo:<c/>"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:7
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"extern void object::Function1( )\n"
"{\n"
"\tSquare(15);\n"
"\tSquare(25);\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"extern void object::Function1( )\n"
"{\n"
"\tSquare(15);\n"
"\tSquare(25);\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:13
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You still have to define the function called <code>Square</code>. In order "
"to do this, you will have to write some instructions outside the <a "
"cbot|bloc>block</a> that until now was the frame of each one of your "
"programs. At the very end of the program, after the last closing brace, we "
"will define the function <code>Square</code>. The program will take the "
"following shape:"
msgstr ""
"Devi ancora definire <code>Square</code>. Scrivila fuori dal <a "
"cbot|bloc>blocco</a> principale, dopo l’ultima graffa. Definiamo lì "
"<code>Square</code>:"

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:15
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"extern void object::Function1( )\n"
"{\n"
"\t<n/>main function ...<code>\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"void object::Square(float length)\n"
"{\n"
"\t</code>new function ...<c/>\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"extern void object::Function1( )\n"
"{\n"
"\t<n/>main function ...<code>\n"
"}\n"
"\n"
"void object::Square(float length)\n"
"{\n"
"\t</code>new function ...<c/>\n"
"}"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let us look in detail at the different elements of the declaration of the "
"function <code>Square</code>:"
msgstr "Vediamo gli elementi della dichiarazione di <code>Square</code>:"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|void>void</a></code>\n"
"This means that this function will return no value."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|void>void</a></code>\n"
"La funzione non restituisce un valore."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:30
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|object>object</a>::</code>\n"
"When you write this in front of the function name, you can have access in the function to all the characteristics of the bot, such as <code>position</code>, <code>orientation</code>, etc. In this exercise, this element is not compulsory, as we will not need the characteristics of the bot in the function."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|object>object</a>::</code>\n"
"Permette di accedere nella funzione alle proprietà del robot, come <code>position</code> e <code>orientation</code>. Qui è facoltativo perché non servono."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:33
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code>Square (  )</code>\n"
"This is the name of the function. You can call it Square, or any other name."
msgstr ""
"<code>Square (  )</code>\n"
"È il nome della funzione: puoi sceglierne anche un altro."

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:36
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<code><a cbot|float>float</a> length</code>\n"
"Here you define the parameters that the function will get when it is called. The first time the function is actually called with <code>Square(15)</code>, the variable <code>length</code> will contain the value <code>15</code>. The second time, <code>length</code> will contain <code>25</code>."
msgstr ""
"<code><a cbot|float>float</a> length</code>\n"
"Definisce il parametro ricevuto. Alla prima chiamata, <code>Square(15)</code>, <code>length</code> contiene <code>15</code>; alla seconda, <code>length</code> contiene <code>25</code>."

#. type: Bullet: '-'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "First the main function <code>Function</code> will be executed."
msgstr "Viene eseguita prima la funzione principale <code>Function</code>."

#. type: Bullet: '-'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:41
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the line <code>Square(15)</code>, the program will follow the red arrow "
"and enter the function <code>Square</code> a first time, <code>length</code>"
" containing <code>15</code>."
msgstr ""
"A <code>Square(15)</code> segue la freccia rossa ed entra in "
"<code>Square</code> con <code>length</code> uguale a <code>15</code>."

#. type: Bullet: '-'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:42
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the end of the function <code>Square</code>, the program follows the "
"orange arrow and comes back to the main function."
msgstr ""
"Alla fine di <code>Square</code> segue la freccia arancione e torna alla "
"funzione principale."

#. type: Bullet: '-'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:43
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the line <code>Square(25)</code>, the program will follow the blue arrow "
"and enter the function <code>Square</code> a second time."
msgstr ""
"A <code>Square(25)</code> segue la freccia blu ed entra una seconda volta in"
" <code>Square</code>."

#. type: Bullet: '-'
#: ../help/help.E.txt:44
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"At the end of the function <code>Square</code>, the program follows the "
"light blue arrow and comes back to the main function."
msgstr ""
"Alla fine di <code>Square</code> segue la freccia azzurra e torna alla "
"funzione principale."

#. type: Image filename
#: ../help/help.E.txt:46
#, no-wrap
msgid "tproc1b"
msgstr "tproc1b"

#. type: Plain text
#: ../help/help.E.txt:47
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the function <code>Square</code>, use the instructions <code><a "
"cbot|move>move</a></code> and <code><a cbot|turn>turn</a></code>. In order "
"to make it shorter, you can use a <code><a cbot|for>for</a></code> loop, "
"that will repeat the instructions <code><a cbot|move>move</a></code> and "
"<code><a cbot|turn>turn</a></code> 4 times; however, this is not compulsory."
msgstr ""
"In <code>Square</code> usa <code><a cbot|move>move</a></code> e <code><a "
"cbot|turn>turn</a></code>. Puoi abbreviare con un ciclo <code><a "
"cbot|for>for</a></code> che ripeta <code><a cbot|move>move</a></code> e "
"<code><a cbot|turn>turn</a></code> 4 volte, ma non è obbligatorio."

#. type: Source code
#: ../help/help.E.txt:49
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"void object::Square(float length)\n"
"{\n"
"\tfor ( int i=0 ; i<4 ; i=i+1 )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmove(length);\n"
"\t\tturn(90);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
"void object::Square(float length)\n"
"{\n"
"\tfor ( int i=0 ; i<4 ; i=i+1 )\n"
"\t{\n"
"\t\tmove(length);\n"
"\t\tturn(90);\n"
"\t}\n"
"}"

